paper square

; --v is the a–c diagonal. --l is the perpendicular bisector of c and a, so
; folding along it maps corner a onto c — which collapses the a–c diagonal to a
; single table point. Referencing the collapsed --v as a line must fail honestly,
; not silently fall back to its stale flat-paper birth line.
mark --v = map .b onto .d
mark --l = map .c onto .a
fold --l moving .a
mark --x = map .b onto --v perp --l

; expect error "collapsed"
